WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.860
Secure IPC in C starts by defining the boundary.

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:13.560
Know which processes may connect, which identity or role they have, who owns the endpoint, how long it exists, and what operations the protocol allows.

3
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.780
A channel that feels local still needs a clear trust model.

4
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:25.540
Restrict endpoint exposure with permissions, least privilege, controlled descriptor and handle inheritance, and predictable cleanup.

5
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:36.360
Named endpoints, shared memory regions, queues, and inherited handles should all be part of the application design rather than accidental side effects of startup.

6
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.800
Validate every message before parsing deeply, allocating, copying, or dispatching actions.

7
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.820
Byte streams need framing.

8
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.240
Lengths and counts need limits.

9
00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:51.660
Unsupported commands and malformed sequences need safe failure.

10
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:59.280
Shared memory needs synchronization, layout contracts, and consistency checks before shared state becomes trusted.

11
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.680
Availability belongs in the security model.

12
00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:08.780
Limit message sizes, queues, connections, shared memory, request rates, and processing time.

13
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.240
Define behavior for slow, malformed, disconnected, or unexpected peers.

14
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.700
Release resources on every path, including interrupted operations and protocol failures.

15
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.700
Finally, use layered assurance.

16
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:30.800
Tests, logging discipline, static analysis, sanitizers, runtime diagnostics, and code review all support IPC safety.

17
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:39.220
The best review traces endpoint creation, peer checks, message validation, dispatch, state changes, cleanup, and error handling.

18
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.640
That trace keeps IPC behavior predictable as systems evolve.
